# The Web Is Yours — Campaign Site Rules

## Project Overview

This repo is the **campaign site** for The Web Is Yours — https://thewebisyours.org

It is **not** the volunteer business template. That lives in a separate repo (`thewebisyours-template`). Do not apply single-file template constraints here.

Contact: hello@thewebisyours.org

## What This Site Is

A multi-page static marketing/ops site:
- Campaign pitch and contact form (home)
- Business onboarding form (`/onboard/`)
- Privacy and terms

Business sites built for clients stay one-page, zero-build, and use the template repo. This campaign site may have multiple pages.

## Stack

- Pure HTML/CSS + minimal vanilla JS
- Shared assets in `css/style.css` and `js/script.js`
- Forms via Web3Forms
- Deploy: Cloudflare Workers static assets (`wrangler.jsonc`, `assets.directory: "."`)
- Local: DDEV (`docroot: "."`) optional

### Never do this (unless explicitly asked)
- Do not add CSS frameworks (Tailwind, Bootstrap, etc.)
- Do not add JS frameworks (React, Vue, Alpine, etc.) or jQuery
- Do not introduce a build tool, Astro, or npm app stack without an explicit request
- Do not add ecommerce, booking systems, or a CMS
- Do not invent campaign policy that contradicts Privacy / Terms

### Always do this
- Keep the site static and deployable as files under the repo root
- Use CSS custom properties in `:root` for colours — no hardcoded hex outside `:root`
- Prefer shared `css/style.css` / `js/script.js` over duplicating chrome across pages
- Write semantic HTML; keep mobile layout working at 375px
- Preserve trailing-slash URLs consistently (`/privacy/`, `/terms/`, `/onboard/`)
- Keep JavaScript minimal and scoped to forms / small UI behaviour

## File Structure

```
index.html           # Campaign homepage
css/style.css        # Shared styles
js/script.js         # Home contact form (role selector, Web3Forms)
onboard/index.html   # Business intake form
privacy/index.html
terms/index.html
favicon.svg
wrangler.jsonc       # Cloudflare deploy config
```

## CSS Architecture

Colours via custom properties in `css/style.css`:

```css
--cream            /* Page background */
--warm-white       /* Surfaces */
--ink              /* Main text */
--mid              /* Secondary text */
--light            /* Muted text */
--terracotta       /* Primary accent */
--terracotta-light /* Accent tint */
--sage             /* Secondary accent */
--sage-light       /* Sage tint */
--border           /* Dividers */
```

Update `:root` for colour changes — do not scatter new hex values inline.

## Fonts

Google Fonts only:
- Lora — headings / logo, serif
- Plus Jakarta Sans — body, sans-serif

Do not add fonts unless asked.

## Pages

1. **Home** (`/`) — header, hero, involvement cards, manifesto, contact form, footer
2. **Onboard** (`/onboard/`) — business application form
3. **Privacy** (`/privacy/`)
4. **Terms** (`/terms/`)

Keep header/footer/nav consistent when editing chrome. Link related flows (e.g. owner path ↔ onboard) when relevant.

## JavaScript

Home (`js/script.js`): honeypot injection, `setRole()`, `scrollToForm()`, Web3Forms submit.

Onboard: page-local script for hours toggles and form submit.

Do not add libraries unless explicitly asked.

## Accessibility

- Interactive elements must be keyboard operable (avoid click-only `div` handlers)
- Labels for form controls; sufficient colour contrast (WCAG AA)
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for decorative animation when touching motion CSS
- Images need descriptive `alt` text

## When Making Edits

- Read the full page/section before editing
- Do not reformat or minify wholesale
- Prefer fixing shared CSS/JS once over copy-paste across pages
- Test mobile after structural changes

## Campaign Values (apply to client business sites)

These constrain what the campaign *offers* businesses — not the shape of this marketing site:

- Domain registered in the business’s name
- One-page business websites via the volunteer template
- Footer credit to thewebisyours.org on business sites
- Hosting on Cloudflare for campaign-built sites

## Related Repo

Volunteer template (zero-build, single `index.html`): `thewebisyours-template`  
Do not migrate that template to Astro or other frameworks.
